# serial_duplex -- the worked example a REPLY needs.
#
# serial_stack is one-way by construction: every client holds read on its
# own receive buffer and holds nothing it may write, so a client can hear a
# delivery and can never answer one. A round trip needs a second region
# owned the other way -- `tx_a`, which client_a may write and the
# virtualiser may only read -- so the answer travels on memory the answerer
# actually holds.
#
# client_b stands beside them holding rx_b alone. It is wired to the
# virtualiser and to no client, so it proves the two refusals a round trip
# invites: a ring across an undeclared channel, and a write into a region
# granted to someone else.
#
# Read whole by `caravan/read.rye`; exercised by `caravan/roundtrip.rye`.

system serial_duplex

domain serial_virt
domain client_a
domain client_b

channel serial_virt client_a
channel serial_virt client_b

region rx_a 4096
region tx_a 4096
region rx_b 4096

grant rx_a serial_virt rw
grant rx_a client_a r
grant tx_a client_a rw
grant tx_a serial_virt r
grant rx_b serial_virt rw
grant rx_b client_b r
